    description: "- **Subject:** A single field name `not_captured` carries two disjoint semantics under two different parents.\n- **Mechanic:** `not_captured` appears under two top-level parents with completely different meanings: under `limits` it lists analysis-coverage gaps (dynamic imports, eval/exec, metaprogramming, …); under `reproducibility_context` it lists reproducibility/determinism gaps (transitive package versions, OS/locale, hardware/floating-point). The two sets are disjoint. Neither is declared in the schema.\n- **Expectation:** One of the two fields should be renamed or otherwise disambiguated so a single name does not denote two unrelated concepts.\n- **Scope:** `limits.not_captured` (6 entries, analysis-coverage gaps) vs `reproducibility_context.not_captured` (3 entries, determinism gaps); the intersection is empty.\n- **Exposure:** A consumer dereferencing `behavior_map.<X>.not_captured` without tracking which parent it came from.\n- **Consequence:** The consumer gets analysis-coverage gaps or reproducibility gaps depending on which parent it dereferenced, with no key in common — silently conflating two unrelated kinds of \"not captured.\"\n\n---\n\n(Filed from dogfooding.)"  # ebe7
    fields: {}  # ebe7
